{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"input_json_delta","partial_json":"}"}},"session_id":"d7b322e9-4ee3-4ff9-8fe4-8bc8d275eec7","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"331e6e55-27e4-49ec-810f-1a23279c670f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfQWy7cWoJpzrdHBbcDQP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011btrobs61p7g8drizefMsT","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"kind":"semantic_job_design_response","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","asset":{"kind":"semantic_stage_asset_candidate","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","statements":[{"statementRef":"design-statement:01-subject-root-and-surface-topology","text":"The subject root is the worksite root \".\". The source paths and the planned command's test paths are relative to that root. The subject is exactly eight authored surfaces at the paths the source gives: specification/project-conformance.md, design/implementation-design.md, package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs and test-execution-plan.json. The execution result is a further surface with no authored file. Everything else in the worksite is non-subject: runtime-owned .abiogenesis/, the job source copy original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt, semantic-assets/, native evidence under execution-evidence/, and the four design-selected verifier scripts under verification/. Each surface is its own target, and no target carries another surface's content. A file existing at its path proves none of its content obligations.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"specification/project-conformance.md\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"design/implementation-design.md\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"package.json\", \"src/hello.mjs\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"design/test-design.md\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"test/component/hello.test.mjs\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"test-execution-plan.json\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Name package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, test-execution-plan.json, and execution result as separate lifecycle surfaces."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Produce no files."}],"requirementRefs":[17],"obligationRefs":[3],"predecessorStatementRefs":[2,20,40]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:02-implementation-realization","text":"src/hello.mjs is a dependency-free ES module. Its only content is the named export function helloWorld(), which directly and synchronously returns the string literal \"Hello, world!\". It has no imports, no default or other export, no async, no console or process use and no top-level side effect. package.json holds exactly \"private\": true and \"type\": \"module\". Name, version, scripts, bin, main, exports, engines and dependencies are left out, so the subject has no CLI, bin, script, HTTP or deployment surface. The greeting reaches a consumer only as the return value. Runner stdout from the node --test commands is verifier-execution output, not subject output.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"src/hello.mjs must export helloWorld() returning exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedStdout: null"}],"requirementRefs":[14,15,16],"obligationRefs":[0,1,2],"predecessorStatementRefs":[37,38,39,16,17,19]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:03-governing-and-design-documents","text":"specification/project-conformance.md declares the project pressure for a JavaScript Hello World software build traversal. It names the seven downstream surfaces using the source's labels and carries the ABG-ownership sentence verbatim, presented as a description of the building environment that grants no authority and puts no runtime in the subject. design/implementation-design.md cites the conformance document as its authority and defines the helloWorld module with its exact return value. It names package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, both verifier paths, test-execution-plan.json and the execution result as separate surfaces. design/test-design.md cites package.json and src/hello.mjs as its evidence source and specifies the component and UAT obligations, including the suite title prefixes. check-documents observes each required element. Faithfulness is left to independent semantic assessment.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Declare the project pressure for a JavaScript Hello World software build traversal."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Name the required downstream lifecycle surfaces: implementation design, source, test design, component test source, UAT test source, test execution plan, and test execution result."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"State that ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Define a minimal JavaScript module that exports helloWorld() returning exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Specify both component and UAT validation obligations."}],"requirementRefs":[18,19,20],"obligationRefs":[4,5,6],"predecessorStatementRefs":[41,42,43,22,23,24]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:04-subject-verifiers","text":"Both verifiers use node:test and node:assert/strict. Each contains the exact statement import { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\", which resolves to the subject module; there is no copy, stub or mock. Each declares exactly one test, which applies assert.strictEqual to the direct return of helloWorld() against \"Hello, world!\". The component test's title begins \"component:\". The UAT test's title begins \"uat:\"; it validates the user-visible greeting contract through the same exported function and adds no CLI or stdout surface. These title prefixes let the single planned run attribute each pass to its suite in the admitted runner output. check-verifiers-and-plan gives these static properties their own admitted execution.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"\"Use node:test and node:assert/strict.\",\n          \"Import the named export exactly as: import { helloWorld } from \\\"../../src/hello.mjs\\\".\",\n          \"Assert helloWorld() returns exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\".\""},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"\"Use node:test and node:assert/strict.\",\n          \"Import the named export exactly as: import { helloWorld } from \\\"../../src/hello.mjs\\\".\",\n          \"Assert the user-visible greeting contract is exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\".\""},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"The component test must import helloWorld and assert the exact return value \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"The UAT test must validate the user-visible greeting contract through the same exported function."}],"requirementRefs":[21,22,14],"obligationRefs":[7,8,0],"predecessorStatementRefs":[44,45,25,18]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:05-execution-plan","text":"test-execution-plan.json holds exactly five keys: command \"node\"; args [\"--test\", \"test/component/hello.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\"]; expectedTestPassCount 2; expectedStdoutMatch \"fail 0\"; assertedReturnValue \"Hello, world!\". It holds no observed value. \"fail 0\" is expected to appear both in the TAP summary (\"# fail 0\") and in the spec-reporter summary with its \"ℹ\" glyph, and it pins no pass count. Each verifier declares one test, so no depth coverage is added, and leaving the pass count unpinned is a permitted conservative choice. The count is fixed at 2 so that the native floor predicate on the planned run uses the plan's value. The plan's \"node\" is realized by the only admitted executable, /opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"The command must be node with args [\\\"--test\\\", \\\"test/component/hello.test.mjs\\\", \\\"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\\\"]."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedStdoutMatch must include stable zero-failure evidence such as fail 0; do not pin an exact pass-count fragment when the generated tests add depth coverage."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"assertedReturnValue must be \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."}],"requirementRefs":[23],"obligationRefs":[9],"predecessorStatementRefs":[46,26,54]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:06-observed-execution-result","text":"The execution result has no file. It is realized by one admitted C2 run, cmd-planned-node-test: the admitted node executable, args identical to the plan's, relativeCwd \".\" and an empty declared environment. The derived fields are defined as follows, and native predicates compute them over that run, separately from the run itself:\n- executionStatus is passed iff p-planned-exit observes exit 0.\n- observedTestPassCount is the value p-planned-pass-count observes against the floor of 2.\n- The stdout digest is the digest the ABI records for that run's stdout.\n- planSatisfied holds iff the command and args equal the plan (declared here and checked by check-verifiers-and-plan), observedTestPassCount ≥ expectedTestPassCount, exit is 0, the admitted stdout contains expectedStdoutMatch, and p-hello-return equals assertedReturnValue.\nNo result file, prewritten success or witness copy is authored.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Produce no files."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan."}],"requirementRefs":[24],"obligationRefs":[10],"predecessorStatementRefs":[47,27,7]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:07-acceptance-predicate-evaluation","text":"The four acceptance conditions are evaluated over the same planned run:\n- The component pass and the UAT pass come from that run's admitted output under the \"component:\" and \"uat:\" titles, with no failing entry.\n- planSatisfied is as defined in design-statement:06.\n- observedTestPassCount ≥ 2 comes from p-planned-pass-count.\ncmd-component-suite-node-test and cmd-uat-suite-node-test (each with pass count ≥ 1 and exit 0) add file-level corroboration from separate runs; they never substitute for the planned run. The TAP-glyph tolerance applies only while p-planned-pass-count and p-planned-exit hold, and it never covers an observed failure. Acceptance remains an owner ruling, and no acceptor is named.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."}],"requirementRefs":[25],"obligationRefs":[11],"predecessorStatementRefs":[48,28]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:08-declared-outcome-observation","text":"The declared return-value outcome gets exactly one typed observation: p-hello-return (module_export_return_exact) on the protected target src/hello.mjs, export helloWorld, equals \"Hello, world!\". The ABI evaluates it in the same turn as the ordered command results. No subject verifier script imports the module to produce it, and neither the plan, a declaration nor a passing assertion stands in for it. check-verifiers-and-plan separately checks that the plan's assertedReturnValue equals the expectedReturnValue it extracts from the job source copy. Because expectedStdout: null declares no stdout outcome, the design declares no stdout predicate for the subject.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedReturnValue: \"Hello, world!\""},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"assertedReturnValue must be \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"src/hello.mjs must export helloWorld() returning exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedStdout: null"}],"requirementRefs":[28,14],"obligationRefs":[14,0],"predecessorStatementRefs":[51,37]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:09-design-selected-checks","text":"The planned run cannot exercise several obligations: the package fields, the no-output-surface constraint, the surface set, the three documents, the static verifier properties, the plan's content, derivation consistency and the no-copy constraint. For these, the design selects four read-only verifier scripts under verification/: check-manifest-and-inventory, check-documents, check-verifiers-and-plan and check-derivation. Each has its own admitted command and an exit-0 predicate. They only read bytes: they never import or execute a subject module and spawn no process. Each prints one JSON line per checked element, with path and sha256, and exits 1 on any failure. They prove presence and consistency, not faithfulness, so independent semantic assessment of the actual bodies is still required.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Specify both component and UAT validation obligations."}],"requirementRefs":[15,16,17,18,19,20,21,22,23,26,27],"obligationRefs":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,12,13],"predecessorStatementRefs":[55,38,39,40,41,42,43,49,50]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:10-derivation-topology","text":"Derivation follows the source's direction: conformance → implementation design → package.json and src/hello.mjs → test design → component verifier → UAT verifier → plan. The result is judged against the plan. Construction is told to author the surfaces in that order within the single construction activation, reading each predecessor's written bytes before writing its dependent. The documents' authority citations make each edge explicit. check-derivation observes each edge's shared facts and prints predecessor and dependent digests at one worksite coordinate. No subject surface exists before the single activation, so no predecessor digest can enter the admitted construction basis through declared read paths. This topology cannot realize the construction-basis clause, which remains a blocking gap (design-pressure:01-derivation-basis-unrealizable).","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior test_design and source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior component_test_source, test_design, and source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior component_test_source and uat_test_source artifact summaries as the evidence source."}],"requirementRefs":[26],"obligationRefs":[12],"predecessorStatementRefs":[49,29,9]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:11-no-copied-machinery","text":"No target copies odd_sdlc runtime code, ledgers, phase-flow controller or local truth surfaces. No subject surface contains runtime, registry, ledger, controller, scheduler or traversal machinery. check-manifest-and-inventory fails in any of these cases:\n- a code surface (package.json, src/hello.mjs, either verifier or the plan) contains odd_sdlc, ledger, phase-flow, controller, scheduler, registry, traversal, child_process or require(;\n- any subject surface contains odd_sdlc or child_process;\n- a code surface imports anything other than node:test, node:assert/strict or ../../src/hello.mjs.\nsrc/hello.mjs imports nothing. The conformance document's ABG-ownership sentence is required content and is permitted.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"do not copy odd_sdlc runtime code, ledgers, phase-flow controller, or local truth surfaces"}],"requirementRefs":[27],"obligationRefs":[13],"predecessorStatementRefs":[50,31]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:12-target-role-mapping","text":"Each target has a single role. Subject product surfaces are implementation targets. The two node:test files and the four verification/ scripts are verifier targets. The test files serve two purposes. They are verifier artifacts for the greeting, execution-result and acceptance obligations, and their bodies are also the realization evidence for the component and UAT verifier obligations. For those two obligations, check-verifiers-and-plan is the static verifier, and the implementation targets are design/test-design.md and src/hello.mjs, the named predecessors the verifiers derive from and import. test-execution-plan.json realizes its own content obligation and is the declared basis for judging the execution result, the acceptance predicate and the declared outcome. Each target's bindingVersionRefs equal the active versions selected by its obligationRefs.","modality":"supporting","sourceQuotes":[],"requirementRefs":[21,22,23],"obligationRefs":[7,8,9],"predecessorStatementRefs":[55,21]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:13-stage-vector-conflict","text":"The per-turn write isolation remains unruled source meaning: the \"Write only\" limits, the \"in this vector\" bans and the plan-stage no-execution limit. executeFromPlan: false is likewise unruled. This design uses one construction activation and derives no per-turn law. Writing the plan executes nothing; only the ABI runs the planned command, during native execution. Whether sequential construction activations are owed is left to an owner ruling, and that ruling could also make the derivation construction-basis clause realizable.","modality":"conflicting","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not write source, tests, package files, or execution plans in this vector."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not execute the test in this vector."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"executeFromPlan: false"}],"requirementRefs":[26],"obligationRefs":[12],"predecessorStatementRefs":[52,30,10]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:14-traversal-parity","text":"witness.parityRule asks for the odd_sdlc eight-step traversal shape to be reproduced as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup. This design does not realize it, and its status remains unruled. The design's native commands are not evidence of an identical legacy traversal. The witness run is neither read nor used as evidence. design-statement:11 carries the rule's no-copy clause.","modality":"conflicting","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup"}],"requirementRefs":[27],"obligationRefs":[],"predecessorStatementRefs":[53,56,33]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:15-execution-capability-and-budget","text":"All seven commands use the single admitted executable, /opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node, with relativeCwd \".\" and an empty declared environment. The three node --test commands use timeoutMs 45000 and terminationGraceMs 1000. The four check commands use timeoutMs 20000 and terminationGraceMs 1000. The summed budget is 222000 ms, or 227000 ms with the 5000 ms owner allowance, which is below both the 300000 ms inactivity limit and the 900000 ms absolute limit. No command declares reports or HTTP launches. dependencyPaths declares only the existing job source copy, which check-verifiers-and-plan reads for expectedReturnValue; it stays read-only and is not a target. dependencyDisposition \"sufficient\" means construction can begin; it is not execution proof.","modality":"supporting","sourceQuotes":[],"requirementRefs":[],"obligationRefs":[],"predecessorStatementRefs":[57]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:16-stage-claim-boundary","text":"This asset designs the destination topology only. No subject surface exists in the current worksite. Nothing has been constructed or executed, and no predicate has been observed. Every obligation stays non-closing until distinct admitted evidence for realization, verifier artifact and verifier execution, plus independent semantic assessment, binds to it. The design infers no acceptance, release or application closure and selects no continuation.","modality":"supporting","sourceQuotes":[],"requirementRefs":[],"obligationRefs":[],"predecessorStatementRefs":[59,36,14]}],"requirementCandidates":[],"worksiteDesign":null,"pressure":[{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:01-derivation-basis-unrealizable","text":"The derivation requirement needs each predecessor's current digest in the dependent's admitted construction basis. This design builds all eight surfaces in one activation, and none of them exists beforehand, so dependencyPaths cannot carry predecessor digests. check-derivation proves only end-state consistency and current digests. The authoring order inside the activation is an instruction, not admitted provenance. Closure of this obligation is blocked until an owner rules on sequential construction activations (req-pressure:01) or the lifecycle offers ordered construction evidence.","requirementRefs":[26],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:02-stdout-fragment-comparison","text":"No native predicate compares a command's stdout with a substring. The check that the planned run's admitted stdout contains \"fail 0\" (the planSatisfied condition and the plan obligation) must therefore be made at the Evidence stage over the admitted stdout. It is not a C2 observation.","requirementRefs":[23,24,25],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:03-same-run-suite-attribution","text":"Attributing the component and UAT passes within the same run depends on the \"component:\"/\"uat:\" titles appearing in the planned run's admitted output. The format of the Node 24.7.0 default reporter has not been observed. The per-suite commands give file-level corroboration, but they are separate runs, and the acceptance predicate does not accept them as a substitute.","requirementRefs":[25,21,22],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:04-reporter-and-count-parsing","text":"Until admitted execution, it is not observed how C2 test_pass_count parses Node 24.7.0 node --test output (spec \"ℹ pass N\" versus TAP \"# pass N\"), nor how the stdout digest is computed. A mismatch will show up as an observed predicate failure; it will not be masked.","requirementRefs":[23,24],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:05-abi-readiness","text":"The design depends on ABI-owned capabilities: C1 construction of the declared targets, C2 execution of the seven commands, the module_export_return_exact observation in the same F_P turn, and evidence admission. This stage does not classify their readiness. Any capability that is not ready blocks the dependent edge as an ABI gap, with no local compensation.","requirementRefs":[28,24,25,14],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:06-single-valued-role","text":"A target's role is single-valued, but the two verifier files are both realization evidence for their own obligations and verifier artifacts for the greeting, result and acceptance obligations. The role mapping in design-statement:12 is an interpretation. Whether the lifecycle accepts it has not been assessed.","requirementRefs":[21,22,23],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:07-stale-requirements-asset-in-worksite","text":"The worksite's semantic-assets/stage-2.json (sha256:bb93b54aed07ea9c68a91d1aa152b80f972d08ee4523ffc0421cc68b0d7d5fc1) is the falsified Requirements candidate, not the admitted Requirements asset semantic-job-asset://abiogenesis/7a978d3cd06835c9a42a81e7ae4fc0c0fd6c5de2d8a4e0ac2880faaa7db45c8f. The design neither reads it nor declares it as a dependency. Construction must take the admitted asset, supplied through context, as its authority.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:08-verifier-sensitivity","text":"No design command shows that the verifiers fail on a wrong greeting. A mutation run was left out because it would need unadmitted nested execution or scratch copies of subject files. Assertion strength therefore rests on the static check and on semantic assessment.","requirementRefs":[21,22],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:09-strict-inventory","text":"check-manifest-and-inventory fails on any file outside the eight subject paths and the declared non-subject roots. A runtime-created file elsewhere would cause an observed failure, which must be recorded, not suppressed.","requirementRefs":[17,27],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:10-open-owner-rulings","text":"These questions remain open for owner rulings, and this design decides none of them:\n- whether per-turn limits survive and sequential activations are owed;\n- traversal-shape parity;\n- artifact summaries versus bodies (this design uses the actual bodies);\n- acceptor identity;\n- repricing of the direct-return reading;\n- whether assertedReturnValue is a separate predicate (this design shares p-hello-return);\n- the meaning of executeFromPlan;\n- whether the predecessor ABG vocabulary fits the current native lifecycle.\nThe witness also remains unverified provenance.","requirementRefs":[26,27,25,28,18,20],"disposition":"conflicting"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:11-unrealized-application-obligations","text":"Every application obligation is still unrealized and unobserved: the eight surfaces, the typed observation, the seven admitted commands and their predicates, the stdout-fragment and per-suite evaluations, independent semantic assessment and the owner acceptance ruling.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:12-revision-cause-unseen","text":"This revision cites cause result result://abiogenesis/cac8a52ee46edd629ceefc1ce6e1a5bd6e475165142a398dee8e6ccfcf47660e, but its content is not in the supplied context. The design does not claim to repair any specific prior defect.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"unassessed"}]},"bindings":[],"design":{"targets":[{"relativePath":"specification/project-conformance.md","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,4,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,4,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this first, before any other subject surface. It is the subject's governing conformance document, in Markdown. It must contain:\n(1) a declaration of the project pressure for a \"JavaScript Hello World software build traversal\", using that exact phrase;\n(2) the seven required downstream lifecycle surfaces, each named with its exact label: implementation design, source, test design, component test source, UAT test source, test execution plan, test execution result;\n(3) this exact sentence: \"ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence.\", followed by a statement that the sentence describes the environment that builds the subject, grants no authority and places no runtime function in the subject;\n(4) a statement that this document is the authority for design/implementation-design.md.\nInclude no source code, test code, package fields or execution-plan values, and do not write the tokens odd_sdlc or child_process."},{"relativePath":"design/implementation-design.md","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,5,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,5,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this second, after reading the written specification/project-conformance.md. It is the subject's own design document in Markdown, not the builder's. It must:\n- cite specification/project-conformance.md as its authority, using the word \"authority\";\n- define the minimal JavaScript ES module src/hello.mjs, which exports the named function helloWorld(); called with no arguments, it directly and synchronously returns exactly \"Hello, world!\", with no Promise, no default or other export, no imports, no output and no side effects;\n- state that package.json contains only \"private\": true and \"type\": \"module\";\n- name each of these as a separate lifecycle surface: package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, test-execution-plan.json, and execution result;\n- state that the execution result has no authored file and is realized only by admitted native execution of the planned command;\n- state that this document is the authority for package.json and src/hello.mjs.\nDo not write the tokens odd_sdlc or child_process."},{"relativePath":"package.json","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[1,2,3,10,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[1,2,3,10,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this third, derived from design/implementation-design.md. Write exactly this JSON object and nothing else: {\"private\": true, \"type\": \"module\"}. Use two-space indentation, keep the keys in that order, and end with a trailing newline. Do not add name, version, scripts, bin, main, exports, engines or any dependency field. This keeps CLI, bin and script surfaces and third-party dependencies out of the subject."},{"relativePath":"src/hello.mjs","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[0,2,3,7,8,10,11,12,13,14],"bindingVersionRefs":[0,2,3,7,8,10,11,12,13,14],"changeInstruction":"Create this together with package.json, derived from design/implementation-design.md. The content is exactly these three lines followed by a trailing newline:\nexport function helloWorld() {\n  return \"Hello, world!\";\n}\nDo not add imports, a default or any other export, async, console or process use, a shebang or any top-level side effect. Both verifiers import this module, and it is the target of the p-hello-return typed observation."},{"relativePath":"design/test-design.md","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,6,7,8,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,6,7,8,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this fourth, after reading the written package.json and src/hello.mjs; cite both files as its evidence source. It is a Markdown test design that specifies both validation obligations:\n- Component: test/component/hello.test.mjs uses node:test and node:assert/strict, imports helloWorld with import { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\", and asserts with strictEqual that helloWorld() returns exactly \"Hello, world!\".\n- UAT: test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs validates the user-visible greeting contract, exactly \"Hello, world!\", through the same exported function, with the same imports, a strict assertion and no CLI or stdout surface.\nState that each file declares one test, that the component test's title begins \"component:\" and the UAT test's title begins \"uat:\", and that these prefixes let the planned run attribute each pass to its suite. The document must contain these strings: helloWorld, Hello, world!, src/hello.mjs, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, component, UAT, same exported function. Do not write the tokens odd_sdlc or child_process."},{"relativePath":"test/component/hello.test.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[0,2,3,7,10,11,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[0,2,3,7,10,11,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this fifth, after reading the written design/test-design.md and src/hello.mjs. The content is exactly:\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"component: helloWorld() returns exactly Hello, world!\", () => {\n  assert.strictEqual(helloWorld(), \"Hello, world!\");\n});\nDo not add other imports, tests, mocks or stubs, and do not use console, process or stdout."},{"relativePath":"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[0,2,3,8,10,11,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[0,2,3,8,10,11,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this sixth, after reading the written test/component/hello.test.mjs, design/test-design.md and src/hello.mjs. The content is exactly:\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"uat: the user-visible greeting contract is exactly Hello, world!\", () => {\n  const greeting = helloWorld();\n  assert.strictEqual(greeting, \"Hello, world!\");\n});\nDo not add other imports, tests, mocks or stubs, add no CLI or stdout surface, and do not use console or process."},{"relativePath":"test-execution-plan.json","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,9,10,11,12,13,14],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,9,10,11,12,13,14],"changeInstruction":"Create this seventh, after reading both written verifier files. Write exactly this JSON object, with two-space indentation, keys in this order and a trailing newline: {\"command\": \"node\", \"args\": [\"--test\", \"test/component/hello.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\"], \"expectedTestPassCount\": 2, \"expectedStdoutMatch\": \"fail 0\", \"assertedReturnValue\": \"Hello, world!\"}. Add no other key. In particular, record no executionStatus, planSatisfied, observed count, digest or other result. Writing the plan executes nothing."},{"relativePath":"verification/check-manifest-and-inventory.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[1,2,3,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[1,2,3,13],"changeInstruction":"This is a design-selected verifier script, not a subject surface; write it after the eight subject surfaces. It is an ES module that imports only node:fs, node:path and node:crypto. It runs with cwd \".\", only reads bytes, never imports or executes a subject module, and spawns no process. For each check it prints one JSON line to stdout (check id, path where relevant, byteLength, sha256, pass boolean, detail), then prints a final summary line. It exits 1 if any check fails, otherwise 0.\nChecks:\n(a) Each of the eight subject paths exists as a regular file; report each file's byteLength and sha256.\n(b) Walk \".\" recursively and classify every file. The eight paths are subject files. Non-subject files are those under .abiogenesis/, execution-evidence/, semantic-assets/ or verification/, plus the file original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt; report non-subject files as counts per root. Any other file fails as unclassified, so no authored execution-result file or extra subject file can exist.\n(c) package.json parses as JSON, with private === true (a boolean) and type === \"module\", and its keys are exactly private and type.\n(d) src/hello.mjs contains no shebang, import, export default, console. or process.; neither verifier contains console., process. or stdout.\n(e) No code surface (package.json, src/hello.mjs, both verifiers, test-execution-plan.json) contains odd_sdlc, ledger, phase-flow, controller, scheduler, registry, traversal, child_process or require(. None of the three documents contains odd_sdlc or child_process. The only import specifiers allowed in code surfaces are node:test, node:assert/strict and ../../src/hello.mjs."},{"relativePath":"verification/check-documents.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[4,5,6],"bindingVersionRefs":[4,5,6],"changeInstruction":"This is a design-selected verifier script, not a subject surface. Follow the same conventions as check-manifest-and-inventory: import only node:fs and node:crypto, read bytes only, print one JSON line per element with path and sha256, and exit 1 on any failure.\n- specification/project-conformance.md must contain the phrase JavaScript Hello World software build traversal; each of the labels implementation design, source, test design, component test source, UAT test source, test execution plan and test execution result (matched case-insensitively); and the exact sentence \"ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence.\"\n- design/implementation-design.md must contain specification/project-conformance.md, authority, helloWorld, Hello, world!, package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, test-execution-plan.json and execution result.\n- design/test-design.md must contain helloWorld, Hello, world!, src/hello.mjs, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, component, UAT and same exported function.\nReport each element separately. This checks presence only, not faithfulness."},{"relativePath":"verification/check-verifiers-and-plan.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[0,7,8,9,14],"bindingVersionRefs":[0,7,8,9,14],"changeInstruction":"This is a design-selected verifier script, not a subject surface. Follow the same conventions: import only node:fs, node:path and node:crypto; never import the subject module; print one JSON line per check, with digests; exit 1 on any failure.\n(a) src/hello.mjs contains export function helloWorld( and the literal \"Hello, world!\", has exactly one export statement, and contains no export default and no async.\n(b) Each verifier:\n- contains the exact text import { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\", and its resolved import path is src/hello.mjs;\n- imports from \"node:test\" and \"node:assert/strict\" and uses no other import specifier;\n- contains strictEqual( and the literal \"Hello, world!\";\n- declares exactly one test( whose title begins \"component:\" in the component file and \"uat:\" in the UAT file.\n(c) test-execution-plan.json parses, and:\n- its keys are exactly command, args, expectedTestPassCount, expectedStdoutMatch and assertedReturnValue;\n- command === \"node\";\n- args deep-equals [\"--test\", \"test/component/hello.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\"], and both files exist;\n- expectedTestPassCount === 2 and is not greater than the number of declared tests;\n- expectedStdoutMatch is a string that contains fail 0 and does not match /pass\\s*\\d/;\n- assertedReturnValue === \"Hello, world!\", and it equals the expectedReturnValue string extracted by regular expression from original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt."},{"relativePath":"verification/check-derivation.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[12],"bindingVersionRefs":[12],"changeInstruction":"This is a design-selected verifier script, not a subject surface. Follow the same conventions: import only node:fs, node:path and node:crypto; read bytes only; exit 1 on any failure. Read all eight subject surfaces once and print their sha256 values as one coordinate. Then, in the source's direction, print one JSON line per edge with the predecessor and dependent paths, their digests and the observed facts:\n(1) conformance → implementation design: the design cites specification/project-conformance.md.\n(2) implementation design → package.json and src/hello.mjs: the design names both paths, helloWorld and Hello, world!; src/hello.mjs exports helloWorld returning that literal; package.json has private true and type module.\n(3) source → test design: the test design names src/hello.mjs and the exported name found in src/hello.mjs.\n(4) test design and source → component verifier: the test design names the file; the file's import resolves to src/hello.mjs and imports a name that src/hello.mjs exports.\n(5) component verifier, test design and source → UAT verifier: the same checks as (4), and the UAT import statement is identical to the component verifier's.\n(6) both verifiers → plan: plan.args after --test equals the two verifier paths, and assertedReturnValue equals the literal in src/hello.mjs and in both verifiers.\n(7) plan → execution result: record that the result is judged only over the admitted run.\nFinally, print a line stating that this check cannot observe construction-basis provenance."}],"dependencyPaths":["original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt"],"dependencyDisposition":"sufficient","commands":[{"commandId":"cmd-planned-node-test","executable":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node","args":["--test","test/component/hello.test.mjs","test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs"],"relativeCwd":".","environment":{},"timeoutMs":45000,"terminationGraceMs":1000,"expectedReports":[]},{"commandId":"cmd-component-suite-node-test","executable":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node","args":["--test","test/component/hello.test.mjs"],"relativeCwd":".","environment":{},"timeoutMs":45000,"terminationGraceMs":1000,"expectedReports":[]},{"commandId":"cmd-uat-suite-node-test","executable":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node","args":["--test","test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs"],"relativeCwd":".","environment":{},"timeoutMs":45000,"terminationGraceMs":1000,"expectedReports":[]},{"commandId":"cmd-check-manifest-inventory","executable":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node","args":["verification/check-manifest-and-inventory.mjs"],"relativeCwd":".","environment":{},"timeoutMs":20000,"terminationGraceMs":1000,"expectedReports":[]},{"commandId":"cmd-check-documents","executable":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node","args":["verification/check-documents.mjs"],"relativeCwd":".","environment":{},"timeoutMs":20000,"terminationGraceMs":1000,"expectedReports":[]},{"commandId":"cmd-check-verifiers-plan","executable":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node","args":["verification/check-verifiers-and-plan.mjs"],"relativeCwd":".","environment":{},"timeoutMs":20000,"terminationGraceMs":1000,"expectedReports":[]},{"commandId":"cmd-check-derivation","executable":"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node","args":["verification/check-derivation.mjs"],"relativeCwd":".","environment":{},"timeoutMs":20000,"terminationGraceMs":1000,"expectedReports":[]}],"outcomePredicates":[{"predicateId":"p-planned-exit","predicateKind":"process_exit","declaration":{"equals":0,"validationCommandId":"cmd-planned-node-test"}},{"predicateId":"p-planned-pass-count","predicateKind":"test_pass_count","declaration":{"greaterThanOrEqual":2,"validationCommandId":"cmd-planned-node-test"}},{"predicateId":"p-component-suite-exit","predicateKind":"process_exit","declaration":{"equals":0,"validationCommandId":"cmd-component-suite-node-test"}},{"predicateId":"p-component-suite-pass-count","predicateKind":"test_pass_count","declaration":{"greaterThanOrEqual":1,"validationCommandId":"cmd-component-suite-node-test"}},{"predicateId":"p-uat-suite-exit","predicateKind":"process_exit","declaration":{"equals":0,"validationCommandId":"cmd-uat-suite-node-test"}},{"predicateId":"p-uat-suite-pass-count","predicateKind":"test_pass_count","declaration":{"greaterThanOrEqual":1,"validationCommandId":"cmd-uat-suite-node-test"}},{"predicateId":"p-hello-return","predicateKind":"module_export_return_exact","declaration":{"path":"src/hello.mjs","export":"helloWorld","equals":"Hello, world!"}},{"predicateId":"p-check-manifest-inventory-exit","predicateKind":"process_exit","declaration":{"equals":0,"validationCommandId":"cmd-check-manifest-inventory"}},{"predicateId":"p-check-documents-exit","predicateKind":"process_exit","declaration":{"equals":0,"validationCommandId":"cmd-check-documents"}},{"predicateId":"p-check-verifiers-plan-exit","predicateKind":"process_exit","declaration":{"equals":0,"validationCommandId":"cmd-check-verifiers-plan"}},{"predicateId":"p-check-derivation-exit","predicateKind":"process_exit","declaration":{"equals":0,"validationCommandId":"cmd-check-derivation"}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":448164,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":448164},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7b322e9-4ee3-4ff9-8fe4-8bc8d275eec7","uuid":"8f48c381-d6d8-4658-a116-219c48e68e03","timestamp":"2026-09-25T17:13:30.908Z","request_id":"req_011CfQWy6rt5jBLctMZgaUQr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011btrobs61p7g8drizefMsT":{"kind":"semantic_job_design_response","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","asset":{"kind":"semantic_stage_asset_candidate","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","statements":[{"statementRef":"design-statement:01-subject-root-and-surface-topology","text":"The subject root is the worksite root \".\". The source paths and the planned command's test paths are relative to that root. The subject is exactly eight authored surfaces at the paths the source gives: specification/project-conformance.md, design/implementation-design.md, package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs and test-execution-plan.json. The execution result is a further surface with no authored file. Everything else in the worksite is non-subject: runtime-owned .abiogenesis/, the job source copy original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt, semantic-assets/, native evidence under execution-evidence/, and the four design-selected verifier scripts under verification/. Each surface is its own target, and no target carries another surface's content. A file existing at its path proves none of its content obligations.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"specification/project-conformance.md\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"design/implementation-design.md\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"package.json\", \"src/hello.mjs\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"design/test-design.md\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"test/component/hello.test.mjs\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"filesToProduce: [\"test-execution-plan.json\"]"},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Name package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, test-execution-plan.json, and execution result as separate lifecycle surfaces."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Produce no files."}],"requirementRefs":[17],"obligationRefs":[3],"predecessorStatementRefs":[2,20,40]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:02-implementation-realization","text":"src/hello.mjs is a dependency-free ES module. Its only content is the named export function helloWorld(), which directly and synchronously returns the string literal \"Hello, world!\". It has no imports, no default or other export, no async, no console or process use and no top-level side effect. package.json holds exactly \"private\": true and \"type\": \"module\". Name, version, scripts, bin, main, exports, engines and dependencies are left out, so the subject has no CLI, bin, script, HTTP or deployment surface. The greeting reaches a consumer only as the return value. Runner stdout from the node --test commands is verifier-execution output, not subject output.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"src/hello.mjs must export helloWorld() returning exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedStdout: null"}],"requirementRefs":[14,15,16],"obligationRefs":[0,1,2],"predecessorStatementRefs":[37,38,39,16,17,19]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:03-governing-and-design-documents","text":"specification/project-conformance.md declares the project pressure for a JavaScript Hello World software build traversal. It names the seven downstream surfaces using the source's labels and carries the ABG-ownership sentence verbatim, presented as a description of the building environment that grants no authority and puts no runtime in the subject. design/implementation-design.md cites the conformance document as its authority and defines the helloWorld module with its exact return value. It names package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, both verifier paths, test-execution-plan.json and the execution result as separate surfaces. design/test-design.md cites package.json and src/hello.mjs as its evidence source and specifies the component and UAT obligations, including the suite title prefixes. check-documents observes each required element. Faithfulness is left to independent semantic assessment.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Declare the project pressure for a JavaScript Hello World software build traversal."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Name the required downstream lifecycle surfaces: implementation design, source, test design, component test source, UAT test source, test execution plan, and test execution result."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"State that ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Define a minimal JavaScript module that exports helloWorld() returning exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Specify both component and UAT validation obligations."}],"requirementRefs":[18,19,20],"obligationRefs":[4,5,6],"predecessorStatementRefs":[41,42,43,22,23,24]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:04-subject-verifiers","text":"Both verifiers use node:test and node:assert/strict. Each contains the exact statement import { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\", which resolves to the subject module; there is no copy, stub or mock. Each declares exactly one test, which applies assert.strictEqual to the direct return of helloWorld() against \"Hello, world!\". The component test's title begins \"component:\". The UAT test's title begins \"uat:\"; it validates the user-visible greeting contract through the same exported function and adds no CLI or stdout surface. These title prefixes let the single planned run attribute each pass to its suite in the admitted runner output. check-verifiers-and-plan gives these static properties their own admitted execution.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"\"Use node:test and node:assert/strict.\",\n          \"Import the named export exactly as: import { helloWorld } from \\\"../../src/hello.mjs\\\".\",\n          \"Assert helloWorld() returns exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\".\""},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"\"Use node:test and node:assert/strict.\",\n          \"Import the named export exactly as: import { helloWorld } from \\\"../../src/hello.mjs\\\".\",\n          \"Assert the user-visible greeting contract is exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\".\""},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"The component test must import helloWorld and assert the exact return value \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"The UAT test must validate the user-visible greeting contract through the same exported function."}],"requirementRefs":[21,22,14],"obligationRefs":[7,8,0],"predecessorStatementRefs":[44,45,25,18]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:05-execution-plan","text":"test-execution-plan.json holds exactly five keys: command \"node\"; args [\"--test\", \"test/component/hello.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\"]; expectedTestPassCount 2; expectedStdoutMatch \"fail 0\"; assertedReturnValue \"Hello, world!\". It holds no observed value. \"fail 0\" is expected to appear both in the TAP summary (\"# fail 0\") and in the spec-reporter summary with its \"ℹ\" glyph, and it pins no pass count. Each verifier declares one test, so no depth coverage is added, and leaving the pass count unpinned is a permitted conservative choice. The count is fixed at 2 so that the native floor predicate on the planned run uses the plan's value. The plan's \"node\" is realized by the only admitted executable, /opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"The command must be node with args [\\\"--test\\\", \\\"test/component/hello.test.mjs\\\", \\\"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\\\"]."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedStdoutMatch must include stable zero-failure evidence such as fail 0; do not pin an exact pass-count fragment when the generated tests add depth coverage."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"assertedReturnValue must be \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."}],"requirementRefs":[23],"obligationRefs":[9],"predecessorStatementRefs":[46,26,54]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:06-observed-execution-result","text":"The execution result has no file. It is realized by one admitted C2 run, cmd-planned-node-test: the admitted node executable, args identical to the plan's, relativeCwd \".\" and an empty declared environment. The derived fields are defined as follows, and native predicates compute them over that run, separately from the run itself:\n- executionStatus is passed iff p-planned-exit observes exit 0.\n- observedTestPassCount is the value p-planned-pass-count observes against the floor of 2.\n- The stdout digest is the digest the ABI records for that run's stdout.\n- planSatisfied holds iff the command and args equal the plan (declared here and checked by check-verifiers-and-plan), observedTestPassCount ≥ expectedTestPassCount, exit is 0, the admitted stdout contains expectedStdoutMatch, and p-hello-return equals assertedReturnValue.\nNo result file, prewritten success or witness copy is authored.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Produce no files."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan."}],"requirementRefs":[24],"obligationRefs":[10],"predecessorStatementRefs":[47,27,7]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:07-acceptance-predicate-evaluation","text":"The four acceptance conditions are evaluated over the same planned run:\n- The component pass and the UAT pass come from that run's admitted output under the \"component:\" and \"uat:\" titles, with no failing entry.\n- planSatisfied is as defined in design-statement:06.\n- observedTestPassCount ≥ 2 comes from p-planned-pass-count.\ncmd-component-suite-node-test and cmd-uat-suite-node-test (each with pass count ≥ 1 and exit 0) add file-level corroboration from separate runs; they never substitute for the planned run. The TAP-glyph tolerance applies only while p-planned-pass-count and p-planned-exit hold, and it never covers an observed failure. Acceptance remains an owner ruling, and no acceptor is named.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."}],"requirementRefs":[25],"obligationRefs":[11],"predecessorStatementRefs":[48,28]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:08-declared-outcome-observation","text":"The declared return-value outcome gets exactly one typed observation: p-hello-return (module_export_return_exact) on the protected target src/hello.mjs, export helloWorld, equals \"Hello, world!\". The ABI evaluates it in the same turn as the ordered command results. No subject verifier script imports the module to produce it, and neither the plan, a declaration nor a passing assertion stands in for it. check-verifiers-and-plan separately checks that the plan's assertedReturnValue equals the expectedReturnValue it extracts from the job source copy. Because expectedStdout: null declares no stdout outcome, the design declares no stdout predicate for the subject.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedReturnValue: \"Hello, world!\""},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"assertedReturnValue must be \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"src/hello.mjs must export helloWorld() returning exactly \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"expectedStdout: null"}],"requirementRefs":[28,14],"obligationRefs":[14,0],"predecessorStatementRefs":[51,37]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:09-design-selected-checks","text":"The planned run cannot exercise several obligations: the package fields, the no-output-surface constraint, the surface set, the three documents, the static verifier properties, the plan's content, derivation consistency and the no-copy constraint. For these, the design selects four read-only verifier scripts under verification/: check-manifest-and-inventory, check-documents, check-verifiers-and-plan and check-derivation. Each has its own admitted command and an exit-0 predicate. They only read bytes: they never import or execute a subject module and spawn no process. Each prints one JSON line per checked element, with path and sha256, and exits 1 on any failure. They prove presence and consistency, not faithfulness, so independent semantic assessment of the actual bodies is still required.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Specify both component and UAT validation obligations."}],"requirementRefs":[15,16,17,18,19,20,21,22,23,26,27],"obligationRefs":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,12,13],"predecessorStatementRefs":[55,38,39,40,41,42,43,49,50]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:10-derivation-topology","text":"Derivation follows the source's direction: conformance → implementation design → package.json and src/hello.mjs → test design → component verifier → UAT verifier → plan. The result is judged against the plan. Construction is told to author the surfaces in that order within the single construction activation, reading each predecessor's written bytes before writing its dependent. The documents' authority citations make each edge explicit. check-derivation observes each edge's shared facts and prints predecessor and dependent digests at one worksite coordinate. No subject surface exists before the single activation, so no predecessor digest can enter the admitted construction basis through declared read paths. This topology cannot realize the construction-basis clause, which remains a blocking gap (design-pressure:01-derivation-basis-unrealizable).","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior test_design and source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior component_test_source, test_design, and source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Use the prior component_test_source and uat_test_source artifact summaries as the evidence source."}],"requirementRefs":[26],"obligationRefs":[12],"predecessorStatementRefs":[49,29,9]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:11-no-copied-machinery","text":"No target copies odd_sdlc runtime code, ledgers, phase-flow controller or local truth surfaces. No subject surface contains runtime, registry, ledger, controller, scheduler or traversal machinery. check-manifest-and-inventory fails in any of these cases:\n- a code surface (package.json, src/hello.mjs, either verifier or the plan) contains odd_sdlc, ledger, phase-flow, controller, scheduler, registry, traversal, child_process or require(;\n- any subject surface contains odd_sdlc or child_process;\n- a code surface imports anything other than node:test, node:assert/strict or ../../src/hello.mjs.\nsrc/hello.mjs imports nothing. The conformance document's ABG-ownership sentence is required content and is permitted.","modality":"normative","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"do not copy odd_sdlc runtime code, ledgers, phase-flow controller, or local truth surfaces"}],"requirementRefs":[27],"obligationRefs":[13],"predecessorStatementRefs":[50,31]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:12-target-role-mapping","text":"Each target has a single role. Subject product surfaces are implementation targets. The two node:test files and the four verification/ scripts are verifier targets. The test files serve two purposes. They are verifier artifacts for the greeting, execution-result and acceptance obligations, and their bodies are also the realization evidence for the component and UAT verifier obligations. For those two obligations, check-verifiers-and-plan is the static verifier, and the implementation targets are design/test-design.md and src/hello.mjs, the named predecessors the verifiers derive from and import. test-execution-plan.json realizes its own content obligation and is the declared basis for judging the execution result, the acceptance predicate and the declared outcome. Each target's bindingVersionRefs equal the active versions selected by its obligationRefs.","modality":"supporting","sourceQuotes":[],"requirementRefs":[21,22,23],"obligationRefs":[7,8,9],"predecessorStatementRefs":[55,21]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:13-stage-vector-conflict","text":"The per-turn write isolation remains unruled source meaning: the \"Write only\" limits, the \"in this vector\" bans and the plan-stage no-execution limit. executeFromPlan: false is likewise unruled. This design uses one construction activation and derives no per-turn law. Writing the plan executes nothing; only the ABI runs the planned command, during native execution. Whether sequential construction activations are owed is left to an owner ruling, and that ruling could also make the derivation construction-basis clause realizable.","modality":"conflicting","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not write source, tests, package files, or execution plans in this vector."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"Do not execute the test in this vector."},{"memberRef":0,"quote":"executeFromPlan: false"}],"requirementRefs":[26],"obligationRefs":[12],"predecessorStatementRefs":[52,30,10]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:14-traversal-parity","text":"witness.parityRule asks for the odd_sdlc eight-step traversal shape to be reproduced as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup. This design does not realize it, and its status remains unruled. The design's native commands are not evidence of an identical legacy traversal. The witness run is neither read nor used as evidence. design-statement:11 carries the rule's no-copy clause.","modality":"conflicting","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":0,"quote":"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup"}],"requirementRefs":[27],"obligationRefs":[],"predecessorStatementRefs":[53,56,33]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:15-execution-capability-and-budget","text":"All seven commands use the single admitted executable, /opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node, with relativeCwd \".\" and an empty declared environment. The three node --test commands use timeoutMs 45000 and terminationGraceMs 1000. The four check commands use timeoutMs 20000 and terminationGraceMs 1000. The summed budget is 222000 ms, or 227000 ms with the 5000 ms owner allowance, which is below both the 300000 ms inactivity limit and the 900000 ms absolute limit. No command declares reports or HTTP launches. dependencyPaths declares only the existing job source copy, which check-verifiers-and-plan reads for expectedReturnValue; it stays read-only and is not a target. dependencyDisposition \"sufficient\" means construction can begin; it is not execution proof.","modality":"supporting","sourceQuotes":[],"requirementRefs":[],"obligationRefs":[],"predecessorStatementRefs":[57]},{"statementRef":"design-statement:16-stage-claim-boundary","text":"This asset designs the destination topology only. No subject surface exists in the current worksite. Nothing has been constructed or executed, and no predicate has been observed. Every obligation stays non-closing until distinct admitted evidence for realization, verifier artifact and verifier execution, plus independent semantic assessment, binds to it. The design infers no acceptance, release or application closure and selects no continuation.","modality":"supporting","sourceQuotes":[],"requirementRefs":[],"obligationRefs":[],"predecessorStatementRefs":[59,36,14]}],"requirementCandidates":[],"worksiteDesign":null,"pressure":[{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:01-derivation-basis-unrealizable","text":"The derivation requirement needs each predecessor's current digest in the dependent's admitted construction basis. This design builds all eight surfaces in one activation, and none of them exists beforehand, so dependencyPaths cannot carry predecessor digests. check-derivation proves only end-state consistency and current digests. The authoring order inside the activation is an instruction, not admitted provenance. Closure of this obligation is blocked until an owner rules on sequential construction activations (req-pressure:01) or the lifecycle offers ordered construction evidence.","requirementRefs":[26],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:02-stdout-fragment-comparison","text":"No native predicate compares a command's stdout with a substring. The check that the planned run's admitted stdout contains \"fail 0\" (the planSatisfied condition and the plan obligation) must therefore be made at the Evidence stage over the admitted stdout. It is not a C2 observation.","requirementRefs":[23,24,25],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:03-same-run-suite-attribution","text":"Attributing the component and UAT passes within the same run depends on the \"component:\"/\"uat:\" titles appearing in the planned run's admitted output. The format of the Node 24.7.0 default reporter has not been observed. The per-suite commands give file-level corroboration, but they are separate runs, and the acceptance predicate does not accept them as a substitute.","requirementRefs":[25,21,22],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:04-reporter-and-count-parsing","text":"Until admitted execution, it is not observed how C2 test_pass_count parses Node 24.7.0 node --test output (spec \"ℹ pass N\" versus TAP \"# pass N\"), nor how the stdout digest is computed. A mismatch will show up as an observed predicate failure; it will not be masked.","requirementRefs":[23,24],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:05-abi-readiness","text":"The design depends on ABI-owned capabilities: C1 construction of the declared targets, C2 execution of the seven commands, the module_export_return_exact observation in the same F_P turn, and evidence admission. This stage does not classify their readiness. Any capability that is not ready blocks the dependent edge as an ABI gap, with no local compensation.","requirementRefs":[28,24,25,14],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:06-single-valued-role","text":"A target's role is single-valued, but the two verifier files are both realization evidence for their own obligations and verifier artifacts for the greeting, result and acceptance obligations. The role mapping in design-statement:12 is an interpretation. Whether the lifecycle accepts it has not been assessed.","requirementRefs":[21,22,23],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:07-stale-requirements-asset-in-worksite","text":"The worksite's semantic-assets/stage-2.json (sha256:bb93b54aed07ea9c68a91d1aa152b80f972d08ee4523ffc0421cc68b0d7d5fc1) is the falsified Requirements candidate, not the admitted Requirements asset semantic-job-asset://abiogenesis/7a978d3cd06835c9a42a81e7ae4fc0c0fd6c5de2d8a4e0ac2880faaa7db45c8f. The design neither reads it nor declares it as a dependency. Construction must take the admitted asset, supplied through context, as its authority.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:08-verifier-sensitivity","text":"No design command shows that the verifiers fail on a wrong greeting. A mutation run was left out because it would need unadmitted nested execution or scratch copies of subject files. Assertion strength therefore rests on the static check and on semantic assessment.","requirementRefs":[21,22],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:09-strict-inventory","text":"check-manifest-and-inventory fails on any file outside the eight subject paths and the declared non-subject roots. A runtime-created file elsewhere would cause an observed failure, which must be recorded, not suppressed.","requirementRefs":[17,27],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:10-open-owner-rulings","text":"These questions remain open for owner rulings, and this design decides none of them:\n- whether per-turn limits survive and sequential activations are owed;\n- traversal-shape parity;\n- artifact summaries versus bodies (this design uses the actual bodies);\n- acceptor identity;\n- repricing of the direct-return reading;\n- whether assertedReturnValue is a separate predicate (this design shares p-hello-return);\n- the meaning of executeFromPlan;\n- whether the predecessor ABG vocabulary fits the current native lifecycle.\nThe witness also remains unverified provenance.","requirementRefs":[26,27,25,28,18,20],"disposition":"conflicting"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:11-unrealized-application-obligations","text":"Every application obligation is still unrealized and unobserved: the eight surfaces, the typed observation, the seven admitted commands and their predicates, the stdout-fragment and per-suite evaluations, independent semantic assessment and the owner acceptance ruling.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"design-pressure:12-revision-cause-unseen","text":"This revision cites cause result result://abiogenesis/cac8a52ee46edd629ceefc1ce6e1a5bd6e475165142a398dee8e6ccfcf47660e, but its content is not in the supplied context. The design does not claim to repair any specific prior defect.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"unassessed"}]},"bindings":[],"design":{"targets":[{"relativePath":"specification/project-conformance.md","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,4,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,4,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this first, before any other subject surface. It is the subject's governing conformance document, in Markdown. It must contain:\n(1) a declaration of the project pressure for a \"JavaScript Hello World software build traversal\", using that exact phrase;\n(2) the seven required downstream lifecycle surfaces, each named with its exact label: implementation design, source, test design, component test source, UAT test source, test execution plan, test execution result;\n(3) this exact sentence: \"ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence.\", followed by a statement that the sentence describes the environment that builds the subject, grants no authority and places no runtime function in the subject;\n(4) a statement that this document is the authority for design/implementation-design.md.\nInclude no source code, test code, package fields or execution-plan values, and do not write the tokens odd_sdlc or child_process."},{"relativePath":"design/implementation-design.md","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,5,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,5,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this second, after reading the written specification/project-conformance.md. It is the subject's own design document in Markdown, not the builder's. It must:\n- cite specification/project-conformance.md as its authority, using the word \"authority\";\n- define the minimal JavaScript ES module src/hello.mjs, which exports the named function helloWorld(); called with no arguments, it directly and synchronously returns exactly \"Hello, world!\", with no Promise, no default or other export, no imports, no output and no side effects;\n- state that package.json contains only \"private\": true and \"type\": \"module\";\n- name each of these as a separate lifecycle surface: package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, test-execution-plan.json, and execution result;\n- state that the execution result has no authored file and is realized only by admitted native execution of the planned command;\n- state that this document is the authority for package.json and src/hello.mjs.\nDo not write the tokens odd_sdlc or child_process."},{"relativePath":"package.json","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[1,2,3,10,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[1,2,3,10,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this third, derived from design/implementation-design.md. Write exactly this JSON object and nothing else: {\"private\": true, \"type\": \"module\"}. Use two-space indentation, keep the keys in that order, and end with a trailing newline. Do not add name, version, scripts, bin, main, exports, engines or any dependency field. This keeps CLI, bin and script surfaces and third-party dependencies out of the subject."},{"relativePath":"src/hello.mjs","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[0,2,3,7,8,10,11,12,13,14],"bindingVersionRefs":[0,2,3,7,8,10,11,12,13,14],"changeInstruction":"Create this together with package.json, derived from design/implementation-design.md. The content is exactly these three lines followed by a trailing newline:\nexport function helloWorld() {\n  return \"Hello, world!\";\n}\nDo not add imports, a default or any other export, async, console or process use, a shebang or any top-level side effect. Both verifiers import this module, and it is the target of the p-hello-return typed observation."},{"relativePath":"design/test-design.md","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,6,7,8,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,6,7,8,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this fourth, after reading the written package.json and src/hello.mjs; cite both files as its evidence source. It is a Markdown test design that specifies both validation obligations:\n- Component: test/component/hello.test.mjs uses node:test and node:assert/strict, imports helloWorld with import { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\", and asserts with strictEqual that helloWorld() returns exactly \"Hello, world!\".\n- UAT: test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs validates the user-visible greeting contract, exactly \"Hello, world!\", through the same exported function, with the same imports, a strict assertion and no CLI or stdout surface.\nState that each file declares one test, that the component test's title begins \"component:\" and the UAT test's title begins \"uat:\", and that these prefixes let the planned run attribute each pass to its suite. The document must contain these strings: helloWorld, Hello, world!, src/hello.mjs, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, component, UAT, same exported function. Do not write the tokens odd_sdlc or child_process."},{"relativePath":"test/component/hello.test.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[0,2,3,7,10,11,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[0,2,3,7,10,11,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this fifth, after reading the written design/test-design.md and src/hello.mjs. The content is exactly:\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"component: helloWorld() returns exactly Hello, world!\", () => {\n  assert.strictEqual(helloWorld(), \"Hello, world!\");\n});\nDo not add other imports, tests, mocks or stubs, and do not use console, process or stdout."},{"relativePath":"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[0,2,3,8,10,11,12,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[0,2,3,8,10,11,12,13],"changeInstruction":"Create this sixth, after reading the written test/component/hello.test.mjs, design/test-design.md and src/hello.mjs. The content is exactly:\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"uat: the user-visible greeting contract is exactly Hello, world!\", () => {\n  const greeting = helloWorld();\n  assert.strictEqual(greeting, \"Hello, world!\");\n});\nDo not add other imports, tests, mocks or stubs, add no CLI or stdout surface, and do not use console or process."},{"relativePath":"test-execution-plan.json","role":"implementation","obligationRefs":[3,9,10,11,12,13,14],"bindingVersionRefs":[3,9,10,11,12,13,14],"changeInstruction":"Create this seventh, after reading both written verifier files. Write exactly this JSON object, with two-space indentation, keys in this order and a trailing newline: {\"command\": \"node\", \"args\": [\"--test\", \"test/component/hello.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs\"], \"expectedTestPassCount\": 2, \"expectedStdoutMatch\": \"fail 0\", \"assertedReturnValue\": \"Hello, world!\"}. Add no other key. In particular, record no executionStatus, planSatisfied, observed count, digest or other result. Writing the plan executes nothing."},{"relativePath":"verification/check-manifest-and-inventory.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[1,2,3,13],"bindingVersionRefs":[1,2,3,13],"changeInstruction":"This is a design-selected verifier script, not a subject surface; write it after the eight subject surfaces. It is an ES module that imports only node:fs, node:path and node:crypto. It runs with cwd \".\", only reads bytes, never imports or executes a subject module, and spawns no process. For each check it prints one JSON line to stdout (check id, path where relevant, byteLength, sha256, pass boolean, detail), then prints a final summary line. It exits 1 if any check fails, otherwise 0.\nChecks:\n(a) Each of the eight subject paths exists as a regular file; report each file's byteLength and sha256.\n(b) Walk \".\" recursively and classify every file. The eight paths are subject files. Non-subject files are those under .abiogenesis/, execution-evidence/, semantic-assets/ or verification/, plus the file original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt; report non-subject files as counts per root. Any other file fails as unclassified, so no authored execution-result file or extra subject file can exist.\n(c) package.json parses as JSON, with private === true (a boolean) and type === \"module\", and its keys are exactly private and type.\n(d) src/hello.mjs contains no shebang, import, export default, console. or process.; neither verifier contains console., process. or stdout.\n(e) No code surface (package.json, src/hello.mjs, both verifiers, test-execution-plan.json) contains odd_sdlc, ledger, phase-flow, controller, scheduler, registry, traversal, child_process or require(. None of the three documents contains odd_sdlc or child_process. The only import specifiers allowed in code surfaces are node:test, node:assert/strict and ../../src/hello.mjs."},{"relativePath":"verification/check-documents.mjs","role":"verifier","obligationRefs":[4,5,6],"bindingVersionRefs":[4,5,6],"changeInstruction":"This is a design-selected verifier script, not a subject surface. Follow the same conventions as check-manifest-and-inventory: import only node:fs and node:crypto, read bytes only, print one JSON line per element with path and sha256, and exit 1 on any failure.\n- specification/project-conformance.md must contain the phrase JavaScript Hello World software build 